{
 "format": "estate-crucible-horror/1",
 "id": "H-0042",
 "title": "DBCS in EBCDIC: SO/SI-delimited words, mixed and G literals, unbalanced and nested shift codes in comments",
 "category": "national",
 "issue": 3816,
 "shapes": [
  "KYUYO01 (cp930, FB80): data names 処理件数 / 見出し / 漢字欄, sections and paragraphs 主処理 / 開始 / 集計",
  "VALUE '給与明細ABC' (mixed literal, shift codes paired)",
  "VALUE G'漢字欄名' (DBCS literal)",
  "comment lines with a Shift-Out never shifted back in, and with two Shift-Outs nested",
  "SHAINREC (cp939, NEL): 社員名 PIC G(10) (20 bytes)"
 ],
 "asserts": "Every DBCS run reads as its characters, each record starts in single-byte mode whatever the previous one left, and a PIC G / PIC N item takes 2 bytes per character.",
 "citations": [
  {
   "doc": "Enterprise COBOL for z/OS 6.4 Language Reference (SC27-8713-03)",
   "section": "User-defined words with DBCS characters (p.12)",
   "url": "https://publibfp.dhe.ibm.com/epubs/pdf/igy6lr40.pdf",
   "quote": "DBCS user-defined words can contain only double-byte characters, and must contain at least one DBCS character that is not in the set A through Z, a through z, 0 through 9, hyphen, and underscore"
  },
  {
   "doc": "Enterprise COBOL for z/OS 6.4 Language Reference (SC27-8713-03)",
   "section": "Alphanumeric literals with DBCS characters (p.40)",
   "url": "https://publibfp.dhe.ibm.com/epubs/pdf/igy6lr40.pdf",
   "quote": "Shift-out and shift-in control characters are part of the literal and must be paired. They must contain zero or an even number of intervening bytes. Nested shift codes are not allowed in the DBCS portion of the literal."
  },
  {
   "doc": "Enterprise COBOL for z/OS 6.4 Language Reference (SC27-8713-03)",
   "section": "DBCS literals (p.41)",
   "url": "https://publibfp.dhe.ibm.com/epubs/pdf/igy6lr40.pdf",
   "quote": "The opening delimiter must be followed immediately by a shift-out control character."
  },
  {
   "doc": "Enterprise COBOL for z/OS 6.4 Language Reference (SC27-8713-03)",
   "section": "Reference modification",
   "url": "https://publibfp.dhe.ibm.com/epubs/pdf/igy6lr40.pdf",
   "quote": "For usages DISPLAY-1 and NATIONAL, each character position occupies 2 bytes."
  },
  {
   "doc": "Enterprise COBOL for z/OS 6.4 Language Reference (SC27-8713-03)",
   "section": "Comment lines (p.60)",
   "url": "https://publibfp.dhe.ibm.com/epubs/pdf/igy6lr40.pdf",
   "quote": "The comment can be written anywhere in the program text area of that line, and can consist of any combination of characters from the character set of the computer."
  }
 ],
 "notes": "#3988's 'mismatched / nested SO-SI' trap lives in comment lines: IBM forbids it in literals, and a comment may hold any characters.",
